// Port of compiler/rustc_serialize/src/opaque/tests.rs.
//
// `Struct` / `Enum` (`#[derive(Encodable_NoContext, Decodable_NoContext)]`) are generated by
// tools/codegen/types.ts (set `rustc_serialize`) into ./tests.gen.ts.
// PORT: the fn-local test types (`UnitLikeStruct`, `A`, `B`) are invisible to the typedefs probe (it
// reads items, not fn bodies), so their derive expansion (serialize.rs `decodable_body` /
// `encodable_body`: a struct's fields in declaration order, no tag) is written out in the tests.
// PORT: `usize`/`isize` are TS numbers (exact up to 2^53): `usize::MAX`/`isize::MIN`/`isize::MAX`
// are the largest exact values instead (leb128/tests.test.ts checks that wider ones are refused).
// The generated types map `u64`/`i64` fields to `number` (typemap.json); the bare `u64`/`i64`
// values are `bigint`.
